label: "ADR 0003: streaming-value I/O for AtomicKeyspace (superseded)"
timestamp: "2026-08-22T20:43:22"
source: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/path/docs/decisions/0003-streaming-value-io.md"
references:
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-kernel-extension"
statement: >
  The proposed v1 design for streaming large values through
  AtomicKeyspace: two representations behind one logical value API —
  inline v2 envelope up to 16 MiB; larger values as a v3 manifest in
  the key object plus immutable fixed-size SHA-256-addressed chunks in
  a kernel-private root; the manifest's conditional PUT the only
  commit point; readers always fetch and validate the control object
  first. Status at birth: PROPOSED / DRAFT — documentation only, no
  implementation authorized. Adjudication did not amend in place: the
  independent adversarial review (SHIP WITH AMENDMENTS) moved to a
  successor record. Superseded by ADR 0004
  (decision-0004-streaming-value-io-v2), which kept the manifest/chunk
  architecture and amended it — this vertex is chain history, not
  live law; read the successor for what stands.
